Here is a main independent claim (Claim 1) formatted according to standard US/WIPO patent conventions, incorporating reference numerals for an apparatus/device claim.

***

**1.** A microfluidic device (100) for purifying target biomolecules (110a) from a heterogeneous fluid sample (108), the device comprising:

a microfluidic channel (102) extending along a longitudinal axis from an upstream end to a downstream end, the microfluidic channel (102) comprising at least one inlet (104, 106) configured to introduce a fluid medium having non-Newtonian viscoelastic properties and the heterogeneous fluid sample (108) containing target biomolecules (110a) and non-target species (110b);

a viscoelastic focusing zone (112) defined within a portion of the microfluidic channel (102), wherein the cross-sectional geometry of the microfluidic channel (102) and the rheological properties of the fluid medium are configured to generate elastic lift forces ($F_E$) acting upon the target biomolecules (110a) and non-target species (110b) to focus said target biomolecules (110a) and non-target species (110b) into one or more pre-aligned focal streams;

an electro-hydrodynamic focusing assembly (114) positioned downstream of, or co-extensive with, the viscoelastic focusing zone (112), the electro-hydrodynamic focusing assembly (114) comprising a plurality of microelectrodes (116a, 116b) disposed proximate to the microfluidic channel (102) and operatively coupled to a power source (118), the plurality of microelectrodes (116a, 116b) configured to generate a spatially controlled electric field within the microfluidic channel (102) to exert electrophoretic and electro-osmotic forces on the pre-aligned focal streams;

wherein the simultaneous superposition of the elastic lift forces ($F_E$) and the electro-hydrodynamic forces differentially shifts the target biomolecules (110a) from the pre-aligned focal streams into a distinct target flow trajectory based on a combination of size, charge, and electrical polarizability, while the non-target species (110b) remain in a separate background trajectory; and

a plurality of outlet channels (120, 122) disposed at the downstream end of the microfluidic channel (102), comprising at least a target collection outlet (120) aligned with the target flow trajectory to collect the purified target biomolecules (110a), and a waste outlet (122) aligned with the background trajectory to divert the non-target species (110b).
